data.content:
**Yes, C# fully supports `stackalloc`'d `Span<nint>` and `Span<nuint>`.** It works without requiring an `unsafe` context — just like any other unmanaged type:

```csharp
Span<nint> span = stackalloc nint[4];
span[0] = 42;
```

This has been supported since C# 9 introduced `nint`/`nuint` as first-class unmanaged types. On this 64-bit system, each `nint` is 8 bytes; on 32-bit it would be 4.
